<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis levels mixed.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis levels mixed.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mixed Wednesday at locations in Kansas and Oklahoma, grain dealers in the High Plains said.</p>
<p>Basis levels eased at some mill locations in eastern Kansas after having shot up on Tuesday. But basis bids at other terminals in Kansas were firmer Wednesday in response to Tuesday's run-up.</p>
<p>&quot;We raised our bids after the mills firmed up in Wichita, Newton, Wellington and Topeka,&quot; said one grain dealer in south central Kansas. &quot;But I don't think it matters how much you raise basis right now. The farmer's just not selling.&quot;  </p>
